WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
In 2024, the official
poverty rate in the United

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.410
States was 10.6 percent.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.070
But that average hides big gaps.

4
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.870
For children, the rate was 14.3 percent.

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.670
And around the world, about 1 in 10 people

6
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.400
live on less than 3 dollars a day.

7
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.270
Now imagine almost every family
in a country gets richer.

8
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:25.190
Could more people end up counted as poor?

9
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:28.350
In this mission, you'll
compare two very different ways

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.070
to draw a poverty line.

11
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.070
Then you'll see how
poverty rates vary by age,

12
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:36.180
by group, and from country to country.

13
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: find out what it
really means to be counted as poor.
